I've left out the `aap:caps/http-client` import and the enrichment fetch. The `with` clause grants this node only `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`, and I can't extend that grant from inside the crate. Adding an outbound call would also send the digest's contents to an external host. If the graph is updated to grant `http-client`, the node can be revised then. The implementation below records each considered id in the `seen` store.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use std::collections::BTreeSet;

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        // Each considered id is marked seen once, however many times it appears.
        let distinct: BTreeSet<&str> = published
            .considered
            .iter()
            .map(|s| s.as_str())
            .collect();

        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        for id in distinct.iter().copied() {
            // The value is the digest date the item was last seen under.
            state_rw::put(id, &published.date);
            recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
        }

        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

